        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दाख़िल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाख़िल — dākhil — \"admitted; entered\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तेज़ बुख़ार की वजह से दादा अस्पताल में दाख़िल हैं। tez bukhār kī vajah se dādā aspatāl meṁ dākhil haiṁ. Grandfather is in hospital with a high fever."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाख़िल (dākhil) is usually traced to Arabic dākhil, \"entering, inside\", which reached Hindi through Persian. aspatāl meṁ dākhil honā is to be admitted to hospital."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
