          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बुलवाना — bulvānā — \"to have someone sent for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दादा की तबीयत बिगड़ी, तो मीरा ने डाक्टर को बुलवाया। dādā kī tabīyat bigṛī, to Mīrā ne ḍākṭar ko bulvāyā. When my grandfather took a turn for the worse, Mira sent for the doctor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने डाक्टर को बुलवाया, usne ḍākṭar ko bulvāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बुलवाना (bulvānā) is the second causative of bolnā: bulānā is \"to call\", and bulvānā is \"to get someone else to call\" a person. CDIAL lists bulānā under bōll, a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 9321)."
            }
          ]
        },
